  "title": "The major 7th chord",
  "summary": "A major triad plus a major 7th: soft and dreamy.",
  "minutes": 5,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Maj7",
      "body": "A major triad with a major 7th on top (11 half steps above the root) is a **maj7** chord. Cmaj7 is C E G B. In a major key, I and IV are maj7 chords.\n\n**Why it matters:** It is the soft, dreamy sound of bossa nova, soul ballads and a lot of neo-soul. Swap I for Imaj7 and a song instantly sounds smoother.",
